R"VG(
# sunlost7.vg (D-05): the rules and the broadcasts of the halls below, a drifter's people's once the sun was going (the root's `dark>=2`): the
# old ages' painted rules on the wall of the warm cave (the ship reading the figures) and the rules written or cut for the halls under the
# mountain (who keeps the fire, who goes up for the ice, the shares, the dead carried up, silence in the deep); the later ages' rules posted in
# the shelters, the announcements of the halls' radio or read out at the shaft (the rations, the heat, the shifts at the warm rock, the air,
# the lights, the children's hours, the deaths), the charter of the deep levels on a drive or a crystal and its amendments. The people's own
# things run through them (their food and drink, their vessels, their fuel, their craft, their games, their sayings), so two peoples' halls
# are not one people's: every pool is a people's share of it.
@apart

genre.deephalls (words=30..165)
  (age<=prehistoric medium=painted|medium=stone) {dh.pt.head} {dh.pt.line} {dh.pt.line} {dh.pt.line} {dh.pt.end}
  (age<=prehistoric medium=painted|medium=stone) {dh.pt.head} {dh.pt.line} {dh.pt.line} {dh.pt.end}
  (age=medieval medium=painted|medium=stone) {dh.cv.head} {dh.wr.item} {dh.wr.item} {dh.cv.close}
  (age=medieval medium=scroll|medium=codex|medium=tablet) {dh.wr.head}\n{dh.wr.item}\n{dh.wr.item}\n{dh.wr.item}\n{dh.wr.close}
  (age=medieval medium=scroll|medium=codex|medium=tablet) {dh.wr.head}\n{dh.wr.item}\n{dh.wr.item}\n{dh.wr.item}\n{dh.wr.item}\n{dh.wr.close}
  (age>=industrial medium=printed) {dh.pn.head}\n{dh.pn.item}\n{dh.pn.item}\n{dh.pn.item}\n{dh.pn.end}
  (age>=industrial medium=printed) {dh.pn.head}\n{dh.pn.item}\n{dh.pn.item}\n{dh.pn.item}\n{dh.pn.item}\n{dh.pn.end}
  (age=modern medium=drive) {dh.pn.head}\n{dh.pn.item}\n{dh.pn.item}\n{dh.pn.item}\n{dh.pn.item}\n{dh.pn.end}
  (age>=industrial medium=cylinder|medium=disc|medium=reel) {dh.bc.open}\n{dh.bc.item}\n{dh.bc.item}\n{dh.bc.close}
  (age>=industrial medium=cylinder|medium=disc|medium=reel) {dh.bc.open}\n{dh.bc.item}\n{dh.bc.item}\n{dh.bc.item}\n{dh.bc.close}
  (age>=industrial medium=drive|medium=crystal) {dh.ch.head}\n{dh.ch.art}\n{dh.ch.art}\n{dh.ch.art}\n{dh.ch.end}
  (age>=industrial medium=drive|medium=crystal) {dh.ch.head}\n{dh.ch.pre}\n{dh.ch.art}\n{dh.ch.art}\n{dh.ch.art}\n{dh.ch.end}
  (age>=industrial medium=drive|medium=crystal) {dh.am.head}\n{dh.am.item}\n{dh.am.item}\n{dh.am.end}

# the halls' own things, a people's few of each
dh.room (people=3)
  main hall
  lower hall
  dining level
  old store
  well room
  long gallery
  stone chamber
dh.stair (people=2)
  the stair
  the shaft
  the long ramp
  the old adit
dh.party (people=2)
  ice party
  stair party
  cold party
  ice crew

# =====================================================================================================================
# the old time: the rules painted on the wall of the warm cave (the ship reads the figures)
# =====================================================================================================================

dh.pt.head (formula people=3)
  (medium=painted) On the wall of {hall.below}, by {warm.ground}, figures in {colour.holy}, in rows the ship reads as rules.
  (medium=painted) Over the place where the fire was kept, a wall of small figures, each doing one thing.
  (medium=painted) Painted at the mouth of {hall.below}, where everyone coming down would see: what is done here.
  (medium=stone) A slab set at the way down into {hall.below}, pecked with figures.
  (medium=stone) A stone by {warm.ground}, its face covered with figures, rubbed smooth at the height of a hand.
  The way of living below, as the {people} drew it.
dh.pt.line (share=0.75)
  (once) A figure feeding a fire of {fuel}, and beside it {n} {dh.pt.small} sleeping: the fire is kept, and the keepers sleep in turn.
  (once) Figures climbing up toward white dots and coming down with blocks on their backs: the ice, carried down from above.
  (once) A row of {vessel}, every one drawn the same size: the shares of the {dark.food}, the same for everyone, the ship thinks.
  (once) A figure lying down, carried by {n} up toward the white dots: the dead are taken up into the cold.
  (once) A figure with its hand over its mouth, by the deepest part of the cave: silence there, the ship thinks.
  (once) The old ones drawn nearest the warm stones, the young further out.
  (once) Hand-prints in {colour.holy} round the fire, many of them, small and large: everyone who swore to keep it.
  (once) The {herd} drawn in a pen at the back, and a figure giving them {dark.food}.
  (once) A circle drawn high up and crossed out; under it the figures going down. Nobody is drawn going back up without ice.
  (once) A child held up to the fire, and the others' hands raised: a child born below, the ship thinks, shown to the fire.
  (once) Two figures fighting, and a third pulling them apart, by the fire: no fighting near the fire.
  (once) Pale shapes drawn growing by the hot stones: the {dark.food} the {people} grew there.
  (once) A figure working {material} by the fire, and others watching: the {craft} went on below.
  (once) {bird} drawn on the wall over the fire, the only ones in the cave: the ship thinks they were painted from memory.
dh.pt.small (pl)
  small figures
  sleepers
  others
dh.pt.end
  The figures stop at the edge of the light the fire would have thrown.
  The last row is unfinished: a fire, and nobody yet beside it.
  Under it all, {motif.over}, the {people}'s own sign.
  The wall is black with soot above the figures; the fire burned here a long time.
  Some figures are painted over newer ones; the rules changed, the ship thinks, or the keepers did.

# =====================================================================================================================
# the halls under the mountain: the rules written (a scroll, a codex, a tablet) or cut in the stone
# =====================================================================================================================

dh.wr.head (formula people=4)
  The rules of {hall.below}, set down at {$seat} by {ruler.the}, for all who live below:
  These are the rules of the halls, to be read aloud at every gathering below:
  How we live in {hall.below}, since the sun went: kept by the keepers of the fire.
  The order of {hall.below}, written so that nobody says they were not told:
  (faith=onegod|faith=manygods) The rules of {hall.below}, under {god}, who is with us in the dark:
dh.cv.head (formula people=3)
  Cut over the door of {hall.below}, for every one who comes down:
  Cut in the stone by {warm.ground}:
  On the great stone at the foot of the stair, cut deep:

dh.wr.item (share=0.7)
  (once) The fire of {fuel} is kept day and night, by turns; whoever lets it go out keeps it alone for a {dh.wr.span}.
  (once) Those who go up for the ice go [in fours and come down in fours|in threes and come down together|in sixes, roped to each other].
  (once) The {dark.food} is shared at the fire, the same to every mouth, [the old and the young alike|a full {vessel.one.n} each|the keepers last].
  (once) The dead are carried up into the cold and laid where the cold keeps them, not {buried} as they were.
  (once) Silence in the deep halls, where the sleepers are[; whoever wakes them keeps the fire|, by the oath of the keepers|, on pain of the stair].
  (once) The warm stones are for [the sick and the newborn first, then the old, then everyone else|the mothers and the newborn, then the sick|the old by night and the children by day].
  (once) No {fuel} is to be burned in the sleeping halls; the air there is for breathing.
  (once) Every one who is able works the beds of {dark.food} by {warm.ground}, a day in every {n}.
  (once) The doors to the surface are shut after the {dh.party}, and the cold kept out.
  (once) The {herd} that are left are kept at the back and fed before anyone eats the seed.
  (once) Nobody goes up alone, for any reason, at any hour.
  (once) The names of the summers are said at {festival}, [so that the children know them|and the oldest says them first|one for every year we had].
  (once) Quarrels are brought to {ruler.the} at the fire and nowhere else.
  (once) Water is melted from the ice at {warm.ground} and carried in the common {vessel}.
  (once) Whoever finds a new warm place in the rock tells the keepers, and it is shared.
  (once) The lamps are lit only in the working halls; the sleeping halls keep the dark.
  (once) The {craft} goes on in the {dh.room}, so that there is work for every hand that is idle.
  (once) No {pastime} in the sleeping halls; at the fire after the meal, as long as the keepers allow.
  (once) Every {garment.n} that is outgrown is given back to the stores for the next child.
  (once) {feast.custom} is kept below as it was kept above, and the {dark.food} shared out for it.
  (once) The {drink} is kept for the sick and the newborn, and for {festival}.
dh.wr.span (people=1)
  month
  turn of the count
  hand of days
dh.wr.close (formula people=3)
  These are the rules. Keep them, and we will be here when the sun comes back, if it does.
  (darkyears>=1) So it is ordered, below {mountain}, in the {#darkyears:ord} year of the dark.
  (dark=2) So it is ordered, below {mountain}, while the sun goes.
  {god.keep}, all of you, below.
  Whoever cannot keep these rules may go up, and see what is there.
  Read this again at the next gathering.
dh.cv.close (formula people=2)
  Keep these, and the fire keeps you.
  These are the rules of the halls. They were cut so that they would last.
  So the {people} live below.

# =====================================================================================================================
# the later ages: the rules posted in the shelters (printed; a modern people's drive the same)
# =====================================================================================================================
)VG"
